Subject: [PATCH] iface-modem: use the SIT port as primary for a SIT-only modem

Target-local patch for the Pixel 9a (google-pixel-9a-tegu-gxq96-mp1-0) on
the Google Kleaf CPIF route, applied after 0001 and 0002. See
targets/boards/google-pixel-9a-tegu-gxq96-mp1-0/s5300-s3-mm-binding.md.

Physical result with 0001+0002 (r5, 2026-11-25): initialization got past
initialization_started() ("no primary AT port: initializing over SIT only")
and then failed in the Modem interface's first step with "Primary port
initialization failed: none found". That step publishes the D-Bus
PrimaryPort and accepts only a QMI, MBIM or AT primary.

When none of those exists, this patch uses the lowest-named non-ignored SIT
port (umts_ipc0) as the primary port. Modems with an AT, QMI or MBIM port
are unaffected.

An audit of the rest of initialization and enabling (Modem, 3GPP, SIM,
firmware, location, messaging, voice, signal, time, SAR) found no other
step that fails fatally without an AT port: the remaining AT-based steps
log and continue, and the fatal ones are SIT-implemented. No SIT protocol
behaviour changes.

diff -ruN a/src/mm-iface-modem.c b/src/mm-iface-modem.c
--- a/src/mm-iface-modem.c	2026-11-25 13:41:34
+++ b/src/mm-iface-modem.c	2026-11-25 13:41:34
@@ -5757,6 +5757,33 @@
             if (!primary)
                 primary = MM_PORT (mm_base_modem_peek_port_primary (MM_BASE_MODEM (self)));
 
+            /* A SIT-only modem (Samsung S5300 on Google's CPIF) has no AT,
+             * QMI or MBIM control port; its SIT control port is the primary
+             * one. Pick the lowest-named non-ignored SIT port so the choice
+             * is stable (umts_ipc0 before umts_ipc1). */
+            if (!primary) {
+                g_autoptr(GList)  sit_ports = NULL;
+                GList            *l;
+
+                sit_ports = mm_base_modem_find_ports (MM_BASE_MODEM (self),
+                                                      MM_PORT_SUBSYS_UNKNOWN,
+                                                      MM_PORT_TYPE_SIT);
+                for (l = sit_ports; l; l = g_list_next (l)) {
+                    MMPort *candidate = MM_PORT (l->data);
+
+                    if (mm_port_get_port_group (candidate) == MM_PORT_GROUP_IGNORED)
+                        continue;
+                    if (!primary ||
+                        g_strcmp0 (mm_port_get_device (candidate), mm_port_get_device (primary)) < 0)
+                        primary = candidate;
+                }
+                /* The modem keeps its own reference to every port. */
+                g_list_foreach (sit_ports, (GFunc) g_object_unref, NULL);
+                if (primary)
+                    mm_obj_dbg (self, "no AT, QMI or MBIM port: using SIT port %s as primary",
+                                mm_port_get_device (primary));
+            }
+
             if (!primary) {
                 g_task_return_new_error (task, MM_CORE_ERROR, MM_CORE_ERROR_FAILED,
                                          "Primary port initialization failed: none found");
